Date: Sat, 12 Sep 2026 16:54:42 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Fix cadence JSON parsing, drop left-accent cards, fix
 Configure overlay bugs
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

1. cadence-builder.ts: buildRecoveryCadence/buildLongTermNurture threw
   outright on any non-strictly-fenced JSON response, with no retry —
   "Win-back cadence generation returned non-JSON output" was a real
   reliability gap, not a fluke. Added callClaudeForJson: extracts JSON
   by bracket-slicing when fence-stripping alone doesn't parse, and
   retries the generation once (with an explicit correction appended)
   before giving up.

2. leak-map-schedule.tsx: the timeline row itself (the actual audit
   list item, not just its outer containers) still had a hardcoded
   bg-white in light mode — fixed to bg-transparent, keeping a translucent
   fill only for the selected row.

3. leak-map-view.tsx: dropped the border-l-2 colored-accent look I'd
   added to the status strip, correlation-flag box, per-metric issue
   tiles, and Data Gaps sidebar — nobody asked for that motif. The
   3 issue tiles now live inside one shared bordered rectangle
   (divide-y between them, no per-row box/tint); Data Gaps and the
   other banners get a plain full border instead of a colored left
   accent.

4. Replaced ActionMenu with a new FloatingPanel (floating-panel.tsx)
   for skill-configure-menu.tsx: ActionMenu closes on any scroll or
   resize event, which fired from scrolling inside its own panel (or a
   mobile keyboard opening) and closed the config form mid-edit.
   FloatingPanel only closes on outside click or Escape, and is wider
   (560px vs 440px) so it reads as a settings panel, not a squeezed
   dropdown. ActionMenu itself is untouched — still correct for actual
   small menus.

